  "id": "bureaucracy",
  "term": "bureaucracy",
  "definition": "In this packet, bureaucracy refers to the organized administrative structure of social service agencies, including oversight by administrators and the way front-line workers carry out services. It is discussed especially in the idea of street-level bureaucracy, which focuses on how workers who directly interact with the public can shape outcomes through their everyday practices.",
